        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(nvidia): sync recommended models with featured catalog",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nKeeps OpenClaw's recommended NVIDIA Endpoint models aligned with NVIDIA's authoritative featured-model catalog instead of leaving users with stale recommendations. The bundled fallback and provider documentation contain only NVIDIA's current five featured models, while authenticated setup and model-selection paths continue pulling the live catalog from NVIDIA's static JSON feed.\r\n\r\n### What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nResolves a problem where NVIDIA Endpoint users could see outdated recommended models and metadata after NVIDIA updated its featured catalog.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Refresh the bundled NVIDIA fallback with Nemotron 3 Ultra, Nemotron 3 Super, GLM 5.2, Kimi K2.6, and Minimax M3 using the values from NVIDIA's featured-model JSON.\r\n- Remove every bundled model row that is absent from NVIDIA's current feed.\r\n- Match feed-provided names and max-output values, normalize Super's bare model ID through the existing NVIDIA prefix rule, and use the published 1,048,576-token context for Nemotron 3 Super.\r\n- Update the NVIDIA provider documentation to match the authoritative catalog.\r\n- Extend NVIDIA catalog, onboarding, and registration tests for the refreshed rows.\r\n\r\n### Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nNVIDIA's public `featured-models.json` is the source of truth for current recommendations. OpenClaw already fetches that feed for authenticated setup and model selection; this change also aligns the bundled unavailable-feed fallback and documentation with the same source.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n### Evidence\r\n\r\n- Live check against `https://assets.ngc.nvidia.com/products/api-catalog/featured-models.json` confirmed the five expected model rows.\r\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/nvidia/provider-catalog.test.ts extensions/nvidia/index.test.ts extensions/nvidia/onboard.test.ts` — 26 tests passed.\r\n- `corepack pnpm docs:check-mdx` — passed.\r\n- `corepack pnpm docs:check-links` — 5,544 internal links checked, 0 broken.\r\n- `corepack pnpm format:docs:check` — passed.\r\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` — passed.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n### User Impact\r\n\r\nNew NVIDIA setup and model-selection flows show the current featured models from NVIDIA's live catalog. If that feed is unavailable, the bundled fallback presents the same five-model set, with Nemotron 3 Super configured for a 1,048,576-token context. Previously bundled model refs that are no longer present in NVIDIA's feed are intentionally removed rather than retained as compatibility-only rows.\r\n",
